cff-version: 1.2.0
message: |
  SpekraVideo is a native iOS camera and real-time Metal spectral film engine
  built on Andrea Volpato's `spektrafilm` and Hanze Qiu's `SpektraLab` C++
  engine core.

  **If you are citing the science, cite spektrafilm, not this.** The physical
  modelling, the profile measurements and the RA-4 print simulation are that
  project's contribution; see the `references` section below and
  https://github.com/andreavolpato/spektrafilm.

  SpekraVideo is GPL-3.0-or-later; the film and paper profiles and the LUTs
  baked from them are CC BY-SA 4.0 and remain Andrea Volpato's work (with 4
  measured B&W profiles by Hanze Qiu). SpekraVideo is an independent open-source
  iOS project and is not affiliated with or endorsed by the spektrafilm or
  SpektraLab projects.

title: "SpekraVideo: an iOS camera for real-time Apple Log spectral film and print simulation"
abstract: |
  SpekraVideo captures 10-bit Apple Log video and 48 MP ProRAW / Bayer RAW still
  photographs on iPhone and develops them in real time through a virtual film
  negative and darkroom print on the GPU using Metal.

version: "1.1.0"
license: "GPL-3.0-or-later"

keywords:
  - "film emulation"
  - "spectral imaging"
  - "color science"
  - "RA-4 print simulation"
  - "Apple Log"
  - "Metal"
  - "iOS"
  - "GPU rendering"

references:
  - type: "software"
    title: "spektrafilm: spectral simulation of analog photography"
    authors:
      - family-names: "Volpato"
        given-names: "Andrea"
    url: "https://github.com/andreavolpato/spektrafilm"
    abstract: |
      The spectral film and print simulation rendered by SpekraVideo. Source of
      the measured film and paper profiles, characteristic curves, DIR-coupler
      and halation models, and the RA-4 print and scan chain.
  - type: "software"
    title: "SpektraLab: a macOS application for spectral film and print simulation"
    authors:
      - family-names: "Qiu"
        given-names: "Hanze"
    url: "https://github.com/JamesQiu2005/SpektraLab"
    abstract: |
      The C++20 port of the spektrafilm spectral engine core and the 4 measured
      black-and-white film profiles.
